<title>UK: Redland shares fall on Capel downgrade.</title>
<headline>Redland shares fall on Capel downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in building materials manufacturer Redland Plc fell sharply on Monday as HSBC Capel cut its earnings forecasts for the group, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares fell 17p to 299-1/2p by 0809 GMT after recovering from a twelve-month low of 297p.  </p>
<p>Market sources said analysts at James Capel had cut earnings forecasts on the back of the group's business prospects in Europe.</p>
<p>--Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
